---
description: Default guidelines
globs: *
alwaysApply: true
---
- Prefer functions/modules over classes; use classes only when needed.
- No Python files in root.
- Tests in tests/, extend existing test files when possible.
- Minimal `__init__.py`; use direct module imports (e.g. `from similarity.mesh.generation import create_cube`), not re-exports.
- Document only when it adds value; skip when code is self-explanatory.
- Run everything with `pixi run`.
- Tests and temp scripts in tests/ only; clean up temp files after use.
- On git commit request: suggest message, let user edit before committing.
- End every text file with a newline.
- No runtime checks for pixi-installed libs.
- Don't reraise exceptions.
- No command line arguments for python files.
- Order within a module: public functions (high-level first) → private helpers (low-level last).
- Imports at top of file only.
- Prefer runtime exceptions over fallbacks/graceful degradation.
